{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdXiziXgxZMe6ekDMmYA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Allen Telescope Array in Northern California now pulls terabits per second of sensor data straight into GPU memory, so observations are processed as they happen and do not have to fill hard drives first. A Holoscan library called DAQIRI handles the transfer, and NVIDIA says the system can sustain 2.4 terabits per second on RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell GPUs, with inference running on premises next to the instrument.\n\nThat architecture is what gives the AI agents built on top of it something to work with. Nexus, a web-based observatory orchestrator that serves as the agent harness, gives them a single source of truth for instrument state, compute resources and pipelines. Researchers can then ask in natural language for jobs such as monitoring packet loss, reading live spectrograms or rewriting a signal-processing block, and the agent acts on the stream while it is still arriving. According to NVIDIA, an agent can also steer the antennae, calibrate and focus the instrument, catch and fix data errors and plot the result. NVIDIA says this compresses work that would take humans weeks or years into hours, but the article offers no comparison or measurement behind that figure.\n\nThe result the article reports is the first real-time AI detection of a pulsar, in the Crab Nebula. Since a pulsar is a known object, my reading is that this demonstrates the pipeline working on a real signal in real time and leaves its performance on unfamiliar signals untested.\n\nThe next step the team describes is evaluating open models, including NVIDIA Nemotron, for cases where data locality and turnaround matter most, and for observatories that may someday run offline on the far side of the moon. Processing data where it is collected and running models beside the instrument is the design that would make such a deployment conceivable, because there would be no raw data stream to ship elsewhere for analysis. The article presents the lunar case only as a possibility under evaluation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1542,"cache_read_input_tokens":2607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1542},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0856093-bf47-4a27-b619-fc92e43c6ae0","uuid":"e4ce4d06-ab35-44d2-8689-a2bc6771a814","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:14:22.896Z","request_id":"req_011CgdXizVswmij1daaotjUw"}
